{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Anti-inflammatory, anti-sepsis, Hemolytic, Antibiofilm, Anticancer", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is most similar (87.5%) to Brevinin-1EMb L: 21%, F=A: 13%. GRAVY: 1.191; mol wt: 2610.268; mol formula: C124H201N29O28S2; mol ex coeff: 125. Chemical modification: C-terminus contains a Rana box: one disulfide bond. Activity: active against Gram+ E. faecalis ATCC 29212 (MIC 3.125 ug/ml), S. aureus ATCC 25923 or MDR ATCC 29213 (MIC 6.25 ug/ml), S. saprophytics ATCCBAA750 (MIC 6.25 ug/mL), S. epidermidis CI 1607BL1D39 (MIC 12.5 uM), S. haemolyticus CI 1607BLD590 (MIC 12.5 ug/ml), Gram- E. coli ATCC 25922 (MIC 100 ug/ml), E. hormaechei ATCC700323 (MIC 100 ug/ml), P. aeruginosa ATCC 27853 (MIC 100 ug/ml), K.pneumoniae ATCC700603 (MIC >100 ug/ml), C. koseri CI 1611SED223 (MIC 50 ug/ml). Thus, mainly Gram+. It also had an effect on biofilms:bacteria:S. aureus. Binds LPS and anti-inflammatory: TNF-alpha, IL-1bta,a nd IL-6 reduced due to peptide treatment at 4 ug/ml. Antimicrobial robustness: heat-stable: MIC didn't change after 1 h incubation at -20oC to 100oC. MOA:bacteria:S. aureus: MOA:bacteria:E. faecalis: membrane permeabilization and damage. In vitro Toxicity: sheep RBC: HC50 35.8 ug/ml. Also toxic to multiple non-cancer cells (IC50 28.34-43.62 ug/ml) and multiple cancer cells (IC50 23.79-39.2 ug/ml).", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "38611812", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Molecules. 2024 Mar 29;29(7):1534. doi: 10.3390/molecules29071534. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP04231", "source_id": "AP04231", "source_numeric_id": "04231", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP04231", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Exploration of the Antibacterial and Anti-Inflammatory Activity of a Novel Antimicrobial Peptide Brevinin-1BW.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
